#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:402
msgid "PEP 380: Syntax for Delegating to a Subgenerator"
msgstr "PEP 380: Syntaxe pro delegovani subgeneratoru"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:404
msgid ""
"PEP 380 adds the ``yield from`` expression, allowing a :term:`generator` to "
"delegate part of its operations to another generator. This allows a section "
"of code containing :keyword:`yield` to be factored out and placed in another"
" generator. Additionally, the subgenerator is allowed to return with a "
"value, and the value is made available to the delegating generator."
msgstr ""
"PEP 380 pridava vyraz ``yield from``, umoznujici :term:`generator` delegovat"
" cast sve operace dalsimu generatoru. To umoznuje sektoru kodu obsahujiciho "
":keyword:`yield` byt vyclenan a umisten v jinem generatoru. Navic je "
"podgenerator dovolen vratit se s hodnotou a hodnota je dostupna delegujicimu"
" generatoru."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:411
msgid ""
"While designed primarily for use in delegating to a subgenerator, the "
"``yield from`` expression actually allows delegation to arbitrary "
"subiterators."
msgstr ""
"Zatimco je primarne navrzeno pro pouziti v delegovani podgeneratoru, vyraz "
"``yield from`` ve skutecnosti umoznuje delegovani libovolnym poditeratorum."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:414
msgid ""
"For simple iterators, ``yield from iterable`` is essentially just a "
"shortened form of ``for item in iterable: yield item``::"
msgstr ""
"Pro jednoduche iteratory je ``yield from iterable`` v podstate jen zkracena "
"forma ``for item in iterable: yield item``::"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:417
msgid ""
">>> def g(x):\n"
"...     yield from range(x, 0, -1)\n"
"...     yield from range(x)\n"
"...\n"
">>> list(g(5))\n"
"[5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4]"
msgstr ""
">>> def g(x):\n"
"...     yield from range(x, 0, -1)\n"
"...     yield from range(x)\n"
"...\n"
">>> list(g(5))\n"
"[5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4]"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:424
msgid ""
"However, unlike an ordinary loop, ``yield from`` allows subgenerators to "
"receive sent and thrown values directly from the calling scope, and return a"
" final value to the outer generator::"
msgstr ""
"Vsak na rozdil od obycejne smycky umoznuje ``yield from`` podgeneratorum "
"prijmout posilane a vyhozene hodnoty primo z vyzyvajiciho opsahu a vratit "
"konecnou hodnotu vnejsšimu generatoru::"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:428
msgid ""
">>> def accumulate():\n"
"...     tally = 0\n"
"...     while 1:\n"
"...         next = yield\n"
"...         if next is None:\n"
"...             return tally\n"
"...         tally += next\n"
"...\n"
">>> def gather_tallies(tallies):\n"
"...     while 1:\n"
"...         tally = yield from accumulate()\n"
"...         tallies.append(tally)\n"
"...\n"
">>> tallies = []\n"
">>> acc = gather_tallies(tallies)\n"
">>> next(acc)  # Ensure the accumulator is ready to accept values\n"
">>> for i in range(4):\n"
"...     acc.send(i)\n"
"...\n"
">>> acc.send(None)  # Finish the first tally\n"
">>> for i in range(5):\n"
"...     acc.send(i)\n"
"...\n"
">>> acc.send(None)  # Finish the second tally\n"
">>> tallies\n"
"[6, 10]"
msgstr ""
">>> def accumulate():\n"
"...     tally = 0\n"
"...     while 1:\n"
"...         next = yield\n"
"...         if next is None:\n"
"...             return tally\n"
"...         tally += next\n"
"...\n"
">>> def gather_tallies(tallies):\n"
"...     while 1:\n"
"...         tally = yield from accumulate()\n"
"...         tallies.append(tally)\n"
"...\n"
">>> tallies = []\n"
">>> acc = gather_tallies(tallies)\n"
">>> next(acc)  # Ensure the accumulator is ready to accept values\n"
">>> for i in range(4):\n"
"...     acc.send(i)\n"
"...\n"
">>> acc.send(None)  # Finish the first tally\n"
">>> for i in range(5):\n"
"...     acc.send(i)\n"
"...\n"
">>> acc.send(None)  # Finish the second tally\n"
">>> tallies\n"
"[6, 10]"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:455
msgid ""
"The main principle driving this change is to allow even generators that are "
"designed to be used with the ``send`` and ``throw`` methods to be split into"
" multiple subgenerators as easily as a single large function can be split "
"into multiple subfunctions."
msgstr ""
"Hlavni princip rizici tuto zmenu je umoznit i generatoru, ktere jsou "
"navrhnuty na pouziti s metodami ``send`` a ``throw`` byt rozdelen na vice "
"podgeneratoru tak snadno jako jedina velka funkce muze byt rozdelen na vice "
"podfunkci."

