"``-``, stejne jako in-place operatory ``+=``, ``-=``, ``|=`` a ``&=``. "
"(Prispel Raymond Hettinger v :issue:`13121`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:1040
msgid "contextlib"
msgstr "contextlib"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.3.rst:1042
msgid ""
":class:`~contextlib.ExitStack` now provides a solid foundation for "
"programmatic manipulation of context managers and similar cleanup "
"functionality. Unlike the previous ``contextlib.nested`` API (which was "
"deprecated and removed), the new API is designed to work correctly "
"regardless of whether context managers acquire their resources in their "
"``__init__`` method (for example, file objects) or in their ``__enter__`` "
"method (for example, synchronisation objects from the :mod:`threading` "
"module)."
msgstr ""
":class:`~contextlib.ExitStack` nyni poskytuje solidni zalozeni pro "
"programove manipulace spravcu kontextu a podobne cisticich funkci. Na rozdil"
" od predchoziho rozhrani ``contextlib.nested`` (ktere bylo zastaralo a "
"odebrano), nove rozhrani je navrzeno pracovat spravne bez ohledu na to, zda "
"spravci kontextu ziskavaji sve zdroje v jejich metode ``__init__`` "
"(napriklad soubory objekty) nebo v jejich metode ``__enter__`` (napriklad "
"synchronizacni objekty z modulu :mod:`threading`)."

